  "interpretation": "Aggregated healing kernels use the existing strictly-faster, below-full-HP healer admission domain. Every stored source successor must be nonterminal with both original actives surviving. Rest-reset HP is retained; non-reset HP translates by the source damage, guarded by the maximum required HP across all stored leaves. A failed guard falls back to ordinary enumeration. Script caps and unresolved probability remain unchanged. Ninety direct probability-map comparisons cover both sides, awake/waking Rest, Sleep Talk, low/full HP, and partial caps; separate cases cover eviction, disabled storage and terminal-source rejection. The control reproduces all prior fixed-work report fields. Two fixed-work arms precede control/healing/healing/control 30-second runs. These are fixed-policy-pair intervals, not unrestricted game value or deployed strength."
